<h1>DocSureInd — System Architecture & Workflow</h1>
<p>DocSureInd (Documents Sure, India) is an AI-powered compliance readiness platform designed for Indian public services. This document outlines the technology stack, software architecture, deployment layers, and end-to-end processing workflows.</p>

<div class="info-box">
  <strong>Key Architecture Principle: Extensible & Multi-Lingual</strong><br>
  DocSureInd leverages Pydantic dynamic dictionary fields, allowing it to be extended to support additional registered document types (Aadhaar, Voter ID, PAN, Passbook, etc.). The client interface is translated in real-time across English, Tamil, and Hindi.
</div>

<h2>1. Technical Stack & Service Placements</h2>
<p>The system is split into an optimized Next.js frontend web interface and a robust FastAPI backend microservice. Below is where each technology is used:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%">Technology</th>
      <th style="width: 15%">Layer</th>
      <th style="width: 25%">Component / File</th>
      <th style="width: 35%">Purpose & Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Next.js 16 (App Router)</strong></td>
      <td>Frontend Web</td>
      <td><code>frontend/app/</code></td>
      <td>Server-side rendering and static page optimizations. Hosts the applications catalog and analysis console.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>React (State hooks)</strong></td>
      <td>Frontend Logic</td>
      <td><code>frontend/app/check/page.tsx</code></td>
      <td>Handles language states, dynamic questionnaire render loop, RAG assistant chat query triggers, and DOM masking.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Web Speech API</strong></td>
      <td>Browser Audio</td>
      <td><code>frontend/app/check/page.tsx</code></td>
      <td>Reads out issues dynamically in Tamil, Hindi, or English using native system SpeechSynthesis voices with fallback safety.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>FastAPI / Uvicorn</strong></td>
      <td>Backend API</td>
      <td><code>backend/app/main.py</code></td>
      <td>Exposes endpoints (<code>/analyze</code>, <code>/templates</code>, <code>/assistant/query</code>, <code>/translate</code>) with async handlers.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Pydantic v2</strong></td>
      <td>Data Models</td>
      <td><code>backend/app/models.py</code></td>
      <td>Validates RAG query schemas, extraction field models, and structures API request/response payloads.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Google GenAI SDK</strong></td>
      <td>AI Engine</td>
      <td><code>backend/app/extraction.py</code></td>
      <td>Integrates Gemini 2.5 Flash model for OCR structured field isolation and grounded guidelines explanations.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>RapidFuzz</strong></td>
      <td>Fuzzy Logic</td>
      <td><code>backend/app/validation.py</code></td>
      <td>Applies fuzzy string token sort ratios to handle reordered name initials and minor spelling variations.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>PyMuPDF & Pillow</strong></td>
      <td>Document Parsers</td>
      <td><code>backend/app/main.py</code></td>
      <td>Parses PDF structures, page limits checking (max 10 pages), and verifies image byte signatures to reject unsupported, spoofed, or structurally invalid uploads.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Pytest</strong></td>
      <td>Testing Frame</td>
      <td><code>backend/tests/</code></td>
      <td>Drives 45 test cases validating rules resolver logic, date of birth transitions, and grounding assistant prompts.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. End-to-End System Workflow</h2>

<h3>Step 1: Service Catalog Selection</h3>
<p>The user selects an application route (e.g. TN Post-Matric Scholarship, fresh Passport, or PAN correction) in the searchable catalogue page. The frontend loads the template requirements and questionnaire questions dynamically from the backend services registry.</p>

<h3>Step 2: Scenario Declaration & Locking</h3>
<p>The user completes eligibility questions. If an unsupported scenario is selected (e.g. Minor for fresh adult passport, or Trust/Firm for individual PAN correction), the UI triggers an alert and disables all file uploads and validation checks, prompting the user to consult official channels.</p>

<h3>Step 3: Signature & Page Verification</h3>
<p>Uploaded documents are run through file signature magic bytes checks (matching expected headers like <code>%PDF</code>, <code>PNG</code>) and page limits to reject unsupported, spoofed, or structurally invalid uploads.</p>

<h3>Step 4: AI Structured Information Extraction</h3>
<p>Gemini 2.5 Flash acts as a multimodal parser, isolating metadata properties into a flexible dictionary registry mapping names, certificate numbers, dates of birth, issue dates, and expiry dates.</p>

<h3>Step 5: Dynamic Rules Resolution & Fuzzy Comparison</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Resolver Logic:</strong> Evaluates questionnaire answers against the template rules (<code>all_of</code>, <code>one_of</code>, <code>conditional</code>, <code>recommended</code>) to construct a custom checklist.</li>
  <li><strong>Correction-Aware Name/DOB Checks:</strong> Cross-compares identities fuzzy-style. If corrections are declared (e.g. name or DOB correction) and supporting certificates (Marriage certificate or Gazette notification) are provided, differences are flagged as manual reviews rather than blocking errors.</li>
  <li><strong>Scoring:</strong> Deducts score values for missing, duplicate, expired, or unreadable documents.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 6: Translation & RAG Explanation</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Instant Translation:</strong> The dropdown selector instantly translates the console (including dynamic form questions, metadata headers, status descriptions, and error guidelines) into English, Tamil, or Hindi.</li>
  <li><strong>Official Grounded Assistant:</strong> If an issue is flagged, clicking the assistant queries <code>/api/v1/assistant/query</code>. The backend retrieves official guidelines from <code>sources.json</code>, queries Gemini under strict grounding parameters, and returns natural language explanations in the user's selected language alongside reviewed official-source URLs and retrieved dates.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 7: Masked Print-ready Report</h3>
<p>The report page dynamically masks sensitive numbers (e.g. <code>••••1234</code> for bank accounts/certificate IDs) and activates print overrides to output a print-friendly readiness report.</p>

</body>
